  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nThe region continues to sit squarely in the middle of upper\nlevel ridging this afternoon. 500mb heights are about 594 dm,\nsurface temperatures are headed back to the upper 90s once again\nwith dewpoints in the low 70s. Noontime heat index readings are\n108 to 112. High based cu are firing at around 6000-7000 ft. A\nsmall shower or few may cook up through late afternoon. Extreme\nheat and humidity persists tomorrow. Although jet- level flow \nshifts to the northwest just enough to give us a little more \nprospect of afternoon showers/thunderstorms. Added a 15-20% \nchance for most of the area in the late afternoon.\n\nA \"cold\" front continues to be advertised for Sunday. There is\nstill a fair chance (40-60%) for 100-105 degree heat index \nvalues for a few hours Sunday morning in the southwestern part\nof the area but the front may slide through just quickly enough\nto prevent that. It will still be hot however, with afternoon\nmaxes in the 91-93 range with dewpoints in the mid 60s. \n\nA pocket of drier air at 850mb or so looks to mix down strongly\non Monday which should help make the humidity quite a bit\nbetter. Max temps will be around 90. Tuesday and Wednesday look\nhot with heat index values pushing back to or above 100 degrees.\nThursday and beyond there is model disagreement on the \nprospects of another front moving through from the northwest. \nDeterministic GFS is the strongest advocate for that in the 12z \nguidance.",
